  "summary": {
    "all_cases_verified": true,
    "case_count": 5,
    "scientific_verdict": "Exhaustive rational evaluation over F_q^n confirms that under m noisy QFT_q^{\\otimes n} dual samples at coordinate noise rate gamma, every non-planted vector x in F_q^n \\ B survives the zero-syndrome intersection cascade with noise-invariant probability q^{-m}, whereas every planted codeword b in B of Hamming weight wt_H(b) survives with probability (1/q + ((q-1)/q)(1 - gamma)^{wt_H(b)})^m, with maximum non-zero survival-to-spurious ratio (1 + (q-1)(1 - gamma)^{d_min(B)})^m governed by the primal minimum distance d_min(B)."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact Weight-Power Survival Law and False-Negative Rate on B",
      "statement": "Under m i.i.d. noisy QFT_q^(tensor n) dual samples u = (v + xi) mod q at noise rate gamma in [0, 1], any planted codeword b in B of Hamming weight wt_H(b) survives all m zero-syndrome checks with exact probability S_planted(wt_H(b); q, gamma, m) = (1/q + ((q-1)/q) * (1 - gamma)^(wt_H(b)))^m."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Universal Noise-Invariance of Non-Planted Spurious Survival on F_q^n \\ B",
      "statement": "For every non-planted vector x in F_q^n \\ B, every noise rate gamma in [0, 1], and every m >= 1, Pr[x in B_hat_(m, gamma)] = q^(-m) identically, so E[|B_hat_(m, gamma) \\ B|] = (q^n - q^d) q^(-m) is independent of gamma."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Primal Minimum-Distance Survival-to-Spurious Frontier",
      "statement": "For any gamma in (0, 1), the m-sample survival-to-spurious ratio Pr[b in B_hat_(m, gamma)] / q^(-m) = (1 + (q - 1)(1 - gamma)^(wt_H(b)))^m over non-zero b in B \\ {0} is maximized at minimum-weight planted codewords wt_H(b) = d_min(B) = min_(b in B \\ {0}) wt_H(b)."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Planted q-ary Noisy Dual-Intersection False-Negative Bridge: Weight-Stratified True-Codeword Survival, Universal Spurious Noise-Invariance, and Primal Minimum-Distance Scaling"
}
